        {
          "status": "announced",
          "summary": "Drewry's Cancelled Sailings tracker shows 39 blanked sailings announced from Week 41 (5-11 October) to Week 45 (2-8 November) across the transpacific, transatlantic and Asia-Europe trades - 5% of 710 scheduled voyages - with half of the blanks on the transpacific. Sea-Intelligence notes the blanking level is low by post-pandemic norms (about 10% of Asia-US west coast sailings are typically blanked), but individual shippers still face rolled sailings, and Drewry warns attention should stay on where carriers make further capacity adjustments after Golden Week demand patterns shift.",
          "headline": "Ocean carriers unveil post-Golden Week blank sailings, half of them on the transpacific",
