        {
          "status": "ongoing",
          "summary": "The Port of Los Angeles reported its best month in history - 1,042,652 TEUs processed in September 2026, a fourth straight month of record volumes driven by retailers frontloading ahead of tariffs. Port executive director Gene Seroka said more containers are already shifting to Los Angeles/Long Beach as the Panama Canal authority begins draft restrictions ahead of an expected severe El Nino season, and he is preparing for about a 5% uptick in containers moving to Los Angeles and Long Beach; November and December volumes are hard to predict. He also flagged California diesel up 62% since February 28, raising inland trucking costs at the nation's highest-in-nation diesel price of $8.36/gallon as of October 9, 2026.",
          "headline": "Record Los Angeles port volumes and Panama Canal draft restrictions set up a container surge at Los Angeles/Long Beach",
