          ]
        },
        {
          "status": "ongoing",
          "summary": "Citing Commercial Times, TrendForce reports a CPU price-hike wave in October: Intel has raised processor prices across product lines starting September 1, with high-end Panther Lake models (whose GPU tiles are made by TSMC on N3E) up 15-20%; Qualcomm raised prices for PC processor platforms including Snapdragon X and X2 Elite by about 10% starting in October; AMD is reportedly preparing adjustments. TSMC is expected to raise foundry prices further in 2027 (analyst forecasts of 5-10% for advanced nodes and 10-15% for advanced packaging), and TrendForce notes continued DRAM and SSD price increases alongside higher CPU costs are putting further pressure on notebook makers even as CPU supply improves.",
