        "US CBP has begun voiding importer-of-record (IOR) numbers where Form 5106 identity data is incomplete - re-reported in The Loadstar's 8 October customs roundup, but the policy took effect in September 2026 (before the window) and was first reported on 2026-09-30, so it fails the first-reported-inside-window rule; it would raise customs risk for the ultrabook's US entries at LA/Long Beach.",
        "ASML reportedly plans a 10% parts price hike in South Korea starting January 2027, with equipment prices possibly also rising (TrendForce, 2026-10-12) - an equipment-cost increase for Samsung and SK hynix, not confirmed as a DRAM/NAND supply disruption for this product.",
